; bml-form-size-band.fk -- one BML form may be as large as the file that
; holds it; the lowering's walker depth does not grow with a form's size.
;
; Witnessed 2026-09-04 on fkwu (ledger R91): `def rows() = list(...)` with
; 60 rows of 500 bytes (about 30 000 normalized characters, a 31 KB file)
; died in the lowering child -- `eval-depth wall — fkwu: eval too deep —
; 266338328 bytes of walker stack (wall 266338304)` -- while 50 rows
; lowered and answered 50. The release ledger's single list() of 90 rows
; crossed the same wall the same day. The walker was source-compiler.fk's
; fsc-bml-normalize-ws-loop, which built its answer as
; (str_concat ch (recurse ...)): a frame per character of the statement,
; string-literal bytes included. It now walks spans as a tail loop.
;
; The fixture holds a single def whose list() is 128 rows of 250 + i bytes
; (40128 bytes, about 40 600 normalized characters -- well past the old
; wall) plus two small defs that pin what normalization keeps. Every
; check reads a value the fixture defines; only natives below (eq, len,
; nth, str_len, str_eq, add, and -- substring and str_find are prelude
; names, not natives, and would fold to nothing here), so no prelude but
; the fixture itself can confound the verdict. A wall returning shows here
; as `bml lowering child failed` and a nonzero exit, never as a quiet
; smaller number.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/tests/bml-form-size-fixture.bml
;
; Expected: 127
;
; bit   1  the list has all 128 rows
; bit   2  the first row arrived whole (250 bytes)
; bit   4  the last row arrived whole (377 bytes)
; bit   8  every row arrived whole: the byte sum is 40128
; bit  16  row 64 sits at position 64 (314 bytes): order survived the lowering
; bit  32  a def with space runs around its params, `=`, args and `;` still binds and adds (2, 3 -> 5)
; bit  64  spaces and escaped quotes INSIDE a literal are kept as written (str_len 8, exact text)

(do
    (defn bfsb-bit (ok bit) (if ok bit 0))
    (defn bfsb-sum-go (xs n)
        (if (eq (len xs) 0) n
            (bfsb-sum-go (tail xs) (add n (str_len (head xs))))))
    (defn bml-form-size-band ()
        (add (bfsb-bit (eq (len (bfs-rows)) 128) 1)
        (add (bfsb-bit (eq (str_len (nth (bfs-rows) 0)) 250) 2)
        (add (bfsb-bit (eq (str_len (nth (bfs-rows) 127)) 377) 4)
        (add (bfsb-bit (eq (bfsb-sum-go (bfs-rows) 0) 40128) 8)
        (add (bfsb-bit (eq (str_len (nth (bfs-rows) 64)) 314) 16)
        (add (bfsb-bit (eq (bfs-spaced 2 3) 5) 32)
             (bfsb-bit (and (eq (str_len (bfs-quoted)) 8)
                            (str_eq (bfs-quoted) "a  b \"c\"")) 64))))))))
    (bml-form-size-band))

; witnessed: 2026-09-04 -> 127
